    {
      "id": "9d4f7b12-3a6e-4c8b-b2d1-7e5a0c3f0020",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -520,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 1,
        "width": 460,
        "height": 940,
        "content": "## Add the missing emails to a dataset you already have\n\n**Who it's for:** you already ran a Google Maps scraper, Places Database or a directory scraper on Apify, and most places have a website but no email.\n\n### How it works\n1. **Email Extractor** (tidytools/website-contact-extractor) reads the dataset by its ID. Places that **already have an email** are not read and not charged (`onlyMissingEmail`). Websites where no email is found are not charged (`requiredContact: email`; set it to `any` to also pay for phone-only results).\n2. Every other website is read once (home, contact, imprint, about pages). Chain branches that share one website are read and charged once, but **each place keeps its own Place ID** and gets its own row.\n3. One row per place goes to Google Sheets: your original email is kept; a new email is added only where there was none.\n\n### Failed websites\nTimeouts and blocked sites are listed in the run's key-value store record **RETRY**. Its `input` is a ready-made input: start the Actor with it (Console: Input > JSON) to try only those places again.\n\n### Dedupe across runs\nWith the same **dedupe name**, a website read in an earlier run (90 days) is returned again without being read or charged.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add your Apify credential to the Apify node and your Google credential to the Sheets node.\n2. In **Dataset settings** paste the **dataset ID** of your scraper run (Apify Console > the run > Storage > Dataset ID). Keep `websiteField` = `website` for Google Maps and Places Database; change it if your scraper names the field differently.\n3. Pick your sheet and click **Execute workflow**.\n\n### Cost\n$2 per 1,000 websites where an email, phone or social profile is found. Places with an email already, places without a website, social pages, unreachable sites and reused websites are free (Apify pay-per-event, Oct 2026). $1 cap on the node; raise it for bigger datasets."
      }
    },
